10
01:00:00,000 --> 01:00:06,000
F1 (marketed as F1: The Movie) is a 2025 American sports drama film starring Brad Pitt as Formula One (F1) racing driver Sonny
Hayes, who returns after a 30-year absence to save his former teammate's underdog team, APXGP, from collapse.

11
01:06:00,000 --> 01:06:06,000
The film was directed by Joseph Kosinski from a screenplay by Ehren Kruger.

12
01:12:00,000 --> 01:12:06,000
Damson Idris, Kerry Condon, Tobias Menzies, and Javier
Bardem also star in supporting roles.

13
01:18:00,000 --> 01:18:06,000
Development of the film began in December 2021 with Pitt, Kosinski, Kruger, and producer Jerry Bruckheimer
attached to the project; the latter three had previously collaborated on Top Gun: Maverick (2022).

14
01:24:00,000 --> 01:24:06,000
Supporting cast members were revealed in early 2023, before the start
of principal photography at Silverstone that July.

15
01:30:00,000 --> 01:30:06,000
Filming also took place during Grand Prix weekends of the 2023 and 2024 World
Championships, with the collaboration of the FIA, the governing body of F1.

16
01:36:00,000 --> 01:36:06,000
Racing sequences were adapted from the real-life races, with F1 teams and drivers
appearing throughout, including Lewis Hamilton, who was also a producer.

17
01:42:00,000 --> 01:42:06,000
Hans Zimmer composed the film's score, while numerous
artists contributed to its soundtrack.

18
01:48:00,000 --> 01:48:06,000
F1 premiered at Radio City Music Hall in New York City on June 16, 2025,
and was released in the United States by Warner Bros.

19
01:54:00,000 --> 01:54:06,000
Pictures and Apple Original Films on June 27.

20
02:00:00,000 --> 02:00:06,000
The film received mostly positive reviews from critics for Kosinski's direction, the racing sequences, visuals,
musical score, and the performances of Pitt and Idris, but deemed the screenplay predictable.

21
02:06:00,000 --> 02:06:06,000
F1 grossed $631.8 million worldwide against a $200–300 million budget, becoming the ninth-highest-grossing film of 2025, the
highest-grossing auto racing film of all time, the highest-grossing film by Apple Studios, and the highest-grossing film of Pitt's career.

22
02:12:00,000 --> 02:12:06,000
The National Board of Review named it as one of the top ten films of the year.

23
02:18:00,000 --> 02:18:06,000
At the 98th Academy Awards, it received four
nominations, including Best Picture.

24
02:24:00,000 --> 02:24:06,000
The film explores themes of comeback, racing, race car
driver, sport competition, beforecreditsstinger.

25
02:30:00,000 --> 02:30:06,000
The tone is emotional.
